# Helm dependency tarballs - fetched fresh via `helm dependency update`,
# which podiumd-minikube provision-cluster already runs as part of setting up any
# cluster this chart deploys to. Originally committed deliberately (matching
# podiumd-infra's own convention) for offline reproducibility without that
# step - reversed once podiumd-minikube provision-cluster existed to run it automatically,
# and once this 3.87MB tarball turned out to be the direct root cause of a
# real bug: Helm's release record embeds the entire resolved chart including
# this dependency, exceeding Kubernetes' hardcoded 3MB API request-size
# limit and forcing `helm install` to be abandoned for `helm template |
# kubectl apply` in the first place (see plan.md's step 4 notes). Chart.lock
# stays committed - it's a small text file (name/version/repository/digest
# only), genuinely useful for pinning without any of the tarball's downsides.
charts/*.tgz

# OS
.DS_Store

# IDE
.idea/

# Python (tests/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.venv/

# Local machine config - direnv env overrides and a local kubeconfig
# directory (KUBECONFIG=/home/kvv/.kube/config.d/minikube, seen live in
# `minikube start` output - can hold cluster credentials, never commit)
.envrc
.kube/

# This developer's own local podiumd/monitoring-logging version selection
# - written by podiumd-minikube set-podiumd-version, read by
# src/podiumd_minikube/dependency.py. Deliberately never committed:
# Chart.yaml no longer holds a real version for either dependency at all
# (see its own comment there), specifically so a personal "let me test a
# different version" choice never shows up as a shared-file diff the way
# editing Chart.yaml directly used to.
.podiumd-versions.yaml

# Written into the working directory by the claude-token-reducer Claude Code plugin.
session_memory.json

# The local CA (src/podiumd_minikube/pki.py); one per checkout, its key never leaves it.
.pki/
# OpenBao's seal key, root token and recovery key (src/podiumd_minikube/openbao.py).
.openbao/
# The rendered Cilium manifest minikube start rereads (src/podiumd_minikube/cni.py).
.cni/
# pg_dumpall backups of Postgres major migrations (src/podiumd_minikube/postgres.py).
.postgres-dumps/
*.egg-info/
